# Maps the identity 61 commits carry to the person who made them.
#
# On 2026-08-20 a subagent set up a throwaway git worktree to test CI's
# generated-file drift guard, changed into it, and gave it a throwaway identity
# with `git config user.email r@r.invalid; git config user.name r`. That is a
# reasonable thing to want in a scratch worktree, and git does not provide it:
# a linked worktree shares .git/config with the repository it belongs to, so
# without `--worktree` the setting is the repository's. Every commit from
# 1d3cd98 (2026-08-20 09:55) to 68c0b42 was authored as "r" before anyone
# noticed.
#
# The commit objects are left alone. They are pushed, three release tags point
# into them, and CI runs and GitHub Releases reference them by hash; rewriting
# 61 commits to correct a name would cost all of that. git log, git shortlog
# and git blame read this file, which is what it is for.
Paul Reitmayer <paul.reitmayer@pm.me> r <r@r.invalid>
